course: dictionary
lesson: 3800
title: The many faces of fore
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word fore has several jobs, so use the context clues to find which one it has. When you shout «Fore!» on a golf course, you are warning people that a ball is flying towards them.
explain: «New stars came to the fore» means the new stars became important and were noticed. On a ship, fore means the front part. In «fore and aft», the fore is the front and the aft is the back.
explain: Fore- can also be a prefix, a word part that goes in front of other words, and it means before or front. In «She grabs him by a fore-leg and a hind-leg», the fore-leg is the front leg. Forehead is the front of your head, and forecast is a prediction made before something happens.
fact: Fore can be an adjective, a noun, an adverb, or a shout: «Fore!»
fact: To come to the fore means to become important or noticed.
fact: «Fore-legs» are the front legs of an animal, as in «he dusted it clean against his fore-legs».
fact: On a ship, fore means at or towards the front, and «fore and aft» means front and back.
fact: The prefix fore- means before or front, as in forehead and foresee.
exercise: «The rabbits held up their fore-paws, and said, "O my!" What are fore-paws? | *Front paws | Soft tails | Back feet | Long ears
exercise: A golfer shouts «Fore!» What is the shout warning people about? | *A ball is flying towards them | A new golf club is here | It is time for lunch | Rain is coming
exercise: «New stars came to the fore.» What does to the fore mean here? | *Became important or noticed | Fell over at the front | Lost in the fog | Went to sleep early
test: On a ship, what is the fore? | The back of the ship | The anchor | The sail | *The front of the ship
test: Which word uses the prefix fore- meaning before? | *forecast | hint | hide | ship
exam: In «fore and aft», which word means front? | *fore | ship | and | aft
